        "1.1": "Substituting $Q_e$ and $\\Phi_B=0$ into [F2] gives $q_e=\\sigma G_Nm_*/c^2=\\sigma m$ and $q_m=0$, while $M=m>0$. Thus $|q_e|=M$ and $f(R)=(1-m/R)^2>0$ for $R>m$. [given, F2, algebra]",
