        "3.1": "The coordinate substitution $T=L\\tau$, $R=Lz$ transforms the limiting pair into $g_{L,z^2}$ and $F_L=\\alpha^{-1}\\mathcal F_L$ from [F3], on $z>0$. Thus the limit is itself a source-free SI model solution. The coordinate scaling uses no choice beyond [A1] and makes no claim about $R=0$. [given, F3, F5, A1, step 2.1, algebra] \u220e"
